## Two things worth your attention

**The template is wrong, not the manifest.** `shared/scope_manifest_template.json` still specifies `reason` for descoped filings. Pipeline v2.9 mandates `descoping_reason` (`mercans_pipeline_v2_9.sh:619`) and auditor C20 keys on it (line 2219). The manifest follows v2.9 correctly — the shared template needs refreshing before the next country, or you'll validate BG/whatever comes next against a stale schema.

**W1 is the one to fix.** `BE-IN-GARNISHMENT-ORDER` has `product_mapping_required=false`, but wage garnishment under Judicial Code Art. 1409 is an in-scope wage type, there's a matching `BE-OUT-GARNISHMENT` outbound leg, and unlike LIMOSA-009 and WACC-010 this entry carries no rationale justifying the `false`. The manifest's own `_note` forbids exactly this. Your spec says WARN not FAIL here, so it doesn't block — but the Art. 1409 attachable-portion bands can't be computed without product mapping. Flip it before Stage 3.

Also carried forward: LIMOSA-009 is in `in_scope` while its A1-posted-worker population is in `employment_types.out_of_scope` (W2); no primary-source schemas exist yet, which will trip auditor C23 at Stage 4 (W4); and the Annex III notional surcharge is asserted at 7% in `special_rules[7]` while `known_limitations[6]` flags it as unconfirmed (W5) — resolve that before any WTC rate depends on it.

